==Films==
===''[[Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania]]'' (2023)===
In ''Ant-Man and The Wasp: Quantumania'', Super Hero partners [[Scott Lang]] and [[Hope van Dyne]] return to continue their adventures as Ant-Man and The Wasp. Together, with Hope's parents [[Hank Pym]] and [[Janet van Dyne]], and Scott's daughter [[Cassie Lang]], the family finds themselves exploring the [[Quantum Realm]], interacting with strange new creatures and embarking on an adventure that will push them beyond the limits of what they thought possible.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/ant-man-and-the-wasp-quantumania-special-look-ccxp22 Special Look at 'Ant-Man and The Wasp: Quantumania' Debuts at CCXP22]</ref>

===''[[Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3]]'' (2023)===
In [[Marvel Studios]]' ''Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3'' our beloved [[Guardians of the Galaxy|band of misfits]] are settling into life on [[Knowhere]]. But it isn't long before their lives are upended by the echoes of [[Rocket Raccoon|Rocket]]'s turbulent past. [[Star-Lord|Peter Quill]], still reeling from the loss of [[Gamora]], must rally his team around him on a dangerous mission to save Rocket's life—a mission that, if not completed successfully, could quite possibly lead to the end of the Guardians as we know them.<ref>[https://thedirect.com/article/guardians-of-the-galaxy-vol-3-rocket-fate Disney Teases Rocket’s Dire Fate In Guardians Vol. 3]</ref>

===''[[The Marvels]]'' (2023)===
In ''The Marvels'', [[Carol Danvers]] aka Captain Marvel has reclaimed her identity from the tyrannical [[Kree]] and [[Battle at Mar-Vell's Laboratory|taken revenge]] on the [[Supreme Intelligence]]. But unintended consequences see Carol shouldering the burden of a destabilized universe. When her duties send her to an anomalous [[wormhole]] linked to a [[Dar-Benn|Kree revolutionary]], her powers become entangled with that of [[Jersey City]] super-fan [[Kamala Khan]], aka Ms. Marvel, and Carol's estranged niece, now [[S.A.B.E.R.]] astronaut Captain [[Monica Rambeau]]. Together, this unlikely trio must team up and learn to work in concert to save the universe as "The Marvels".<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/movies/marvels-teaser-trailer-carol-danvers-monica-rambeau-kamala-khan 'The Marvels': New Teaser Trailer Sends Carol Danvers, Monica Rambeau, and Kamala Khan on a Cosmic Adventure]</ref>

===''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024)===
[[Marvel Studios]] presents their most significant mistake to date—"Deadpool & Wolverine." A listless [[Wade Wilson]] toils away in civilian life. His days as the morally flexible mercenary, Deadpool, behind him. When his homeworld faces an existential threat, Wade must reluctantly suit-up again with an even more reluctantlier… reluctanter? Reluctantest? He must convince a reluctant [[Wolverine]] to— ''Fuck''. Synopses are so fucking stupid.<ref>[https://dam.gettyimages.com/thewaltdisneystudios/deadpoolwolverine/#!asset/b5tx8p3cshmx9s9r5g4pkz83 DEADPOOL WOLVERINE Synopsis REV 5-16-24.pdf]</ref>

===''[[Captain America: Brave New World]]'' (2025)===
After meeting with newly elected [[United States of America|U.S.]] President [[Thaddeus Ross]], [[Sam Wilson|Sam]] finds himself in the middle of an international incident. He must discover the reason behind a nefarious global plot before the true mastermind has the entire world seeing red.<ref>[https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/captain-america-brave-new-world-teaser-trailer/ ‘Captain America: Brave New World’: Here’s the New Teaser Trailer from Marvel Studios]</ref>

===''[[Thunderbolts*]]'' (2025)===
[[Marvel Studios]] (and a crew of indie veterans who definitely sold out) present ''Thunderbolts*'', an irreverent team-up featuring depressed assassin [[Yelena Belova]] alongside the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe|MCU]]'s least anticipated [[Thunderbolts|band of misfits]].<ref>[https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/marvel-studios-announces-robert-downey-jr-and-the-russo-brothers-to-return-for-avengers-doomsday/ Marvel Studios Announces Robert Downey Jr. and the Russo Brothers to Return for ‘Avengers: Doomsday’]</ref>

==Television Series==
===''[[Secret Invasion (TV series)|Secret Invasion]]'' (2023)===
====[[Secret Invasion  (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2023)====
In ''Secret Invasion'', set in the [[2026|present-day]] [[Marvel Cinematic Universe|MCU]], [[Nick Fury|Fury]] learns of a clandestine [[Secret Invasion|invasion]] of [[Earth]] by a [[Skrull Resistance|faction]] of shapeshifting [[Skrulls]]. Fury joins his allies, including [[Everett Ross]], [[Maria Hill]], and the Skrull [[Talos]], who has made a life for himself on Earth. Together they race against time to thwart an imminent Skrull invasion and save [[Humans|humanity]].<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/secret-invasion-trailer-poster Trust No One in the New Trailer for 'Secret Invasion']</ref>

===''[[I Am Groot]]'' (2022-2023)===
====[[I Am Groot/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
The troublemaking twig returns to mischief in the second season of ''I Am Groot''. This time, Baby [[Groot]] finds himself exploring the universe and beyond aboard the [[Guardians of the Galaxy|Guardians]]' spaceships, coming face-to-face—or nose-to-nose—with new and colorful creatures and environments.<ref>[https://whatsondisneyplus.com/marvels-i-am-groot-season-2-trailer-released-disney-release-date-announced/ Marvel’s “I Am Groot” Season 2 Trailer Released & Disney+ Release Date Announced]</ref>

===''[[Loki (TV series)|Loki]]'' (2021-2023)===
====[[Loki (TV series)/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
''Loki'' Season 2 picks up in the aftermath of the shocking season finale when [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] finds himself in a battle for the soul of the [[Time Variance Authority]]. Along with [[Mobius M. Mobius]], [[Hunter B-15]] and a team of new and returning characters, Loki navigates an ever-expanding and increasingly dangerous [[multiverse]] in search of [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Sylvie]], Judge [[Ravonna Renslayer|Renslayer]], [[Miss Minutes]] and the truth of what it means to possess free will and glorious purpose.<ref name="Loki Season Two Synopsis">[https://coveredgeekly.com/new-loki-season-2-cast-members-extended-synopsis-revealed/ New ‘Loki’ Season 2 Cast Members, Extended Synopsis Revealed]</ref>

===''[[What If...?]]'' (2021-TBA)===
====[[What If...?/Season Two|Season Two]] (2023)====
[[What If...?/Season Two|Season 2]] of ''What If...?'' continues the journey as [[The Watcher]] guides viewers through the vast [[Multiverse]], introducing brand new and familiar faces throughout the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]]. The series questions, revisits and twists classic Marvel Cinematic moments with an incredible voice cast that includes a host of stars who reprise their iconic roles.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/what-if-season-2-trailer ‘What If…?’: Unwrap New Season 2 Trailer Now]</ref>

===''[[Echo (TV series)|Echo]]'' (2024)===
====[[Echo (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
''Echo'' spotlights [[Maya Lopez]] as she is pursued by [[Wilson Fisk]]'s criminal empire. When the journey brings her home, she must confront her own family and legacy.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/echo-director-sydney-freeland-maya-lopez-kingpin ‘Echo’ Director Sydney Freeland Teases What’s Ahead for Maya Lopez]</ref>

===''[[Agatha All Along (TV series)|Agatha All Along]]'' (2024)===
====[[Agatha All Along (TV series)/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
[[Marvel Studios]] presents ''Agatha'' in which we see [[Agatha Harkness]] finally break out of a spell she has been trapped in. She can’t wait to go back to her old murderous ways only to find that she is powerless. The only way forward for her is to embark on a perilous quest to get her powers back with the help of an unlikely friend or two.<ref>[https://cocatalog.loc.gov/cgi-bin/Pwebrecon.cgi?Search_Arg=agatha+episode&Search_Code=TALL&PID=7y1AKwit7xtUnlGeY876j2eG1cr3&SEQ=20231006102205&CNT=25&HIST=1 Agatha - U.S. Copyright Office]</ref>

===''[[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man]]'' (2024)===
====[[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
[[Marvel Studios]] presents ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' in which Peter Parker's life, while getting ready for his High School orientation, is forever changed by events that send him on a journey like none before.<ref>[https://cocatalog.loc.gov/cgi-bin/Pwebrecon.cgi?Search_Arg=spider-man%3A+freshman+year&Search_Code=TALL&PID=HkvC2TAKWtjAoBvC2XblG0blGf9&SEQ=20231006110449&CNT=25&HIST=1 Spider-Man: Freshman Year - U.S. Copyright Office]</ref>

===''[[Eyes of Wakanda]]'' (2024)===
====[[Eyes of Wakanda/Season One|Season One]] (2024)====
Throughout [[Wakanda]]n history, brave warriors have been tasked to travel the world retrieving dangerous [[vibranium]] artifacts. This is their story.<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/marvel-studios-animation-what-if-season-2 Marvel Studios Celebrates New Season of 'What If...?']</ref>

===''[[Daredevil: Born Again]]'' (2025)===
====[[Daredevil: Born Again/Season One|Season One]] (2025)====
[[Marvel Studios]] presents ''Daredevil'' in which longtime rivals [[Matt Murdock]] and [[Wilson Fisk]] try to leave behind their darker alter-egos to serve the people of [[New York City|New York]] only to have their pasts catch up to them.<ref>[https://cocatalog.loc.gov/cgi-bin/Pwebrecon.cgi?v1=8&ti=1,8&Search%5FArg=daredevil%20born%20again&Search%5FCode=TALL&CNT=25&PID=Z2dIdDImyfeYjH7L1LJMgMEHv&SEQ=20231006103435&SID=1 Daredevil: Born Again - U.S. Copyright Office]</ref>

===''[[Marvel Zombies]]'' (TBA)===
====[[Marvel Zombies/Season One|Season One]] (TBA)====
The animated series from [[Marvel Studios]] reimagines the Marvel Universe as a new generation of heroes battle against an ever-spreading [[Zombies|zombie]] [[Quantum Virus|scourge]].<ref>[https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/zombies-animated-disney-plus Disney+ Day 2021: Animated ‘Marvel Zombies’ Announced]</ref>

